WEBVTT

00:00.120 --> 00:02.970
-: So far with git stash, we've put one thing

00:02.970 --> 00:05.310
in the stash and then popped it out, right?

00:05.310 --> 00:08.550
One set of changes and then we popped or applied it,

00:08.550 --> 00:11.460
but we can actually stash again and again.

00:11.460 --> 00:14.880
We can have multiple stashes in our stack of stashes,

00:14.880 --> 00:18.360
and they will be kept in the order that we added them in.

00:18.360 --> 00:19.260
I've gotta be honest though,

00:19.260 --> 00:22.440
I don't do this really, at least not frequently.

00:22.440 --> 00:25.350
Like I said, 99 or 90 something percent of the time,

00:25.350 --> 00:27.780
I'm just doing git stash and git stash pop.

00:27.780 --> 00:30.780
But I'm being comprehensive, or at least attempting to.

00:30.780 --> 00:32.580
So I'll show this very quickly.

00:32.580 --> 00:36.870
Well, relatively quickly, I'm going to make a new branch.

00:36.870 --> 00:40.140
So I am on this magenta, no, I'm on the goodbye branch.

00:40.140 --> 00:45.140
We'll just add those changes and commit now, commit dash m.

00:45.450 --> 00:48.300
Let's just do change to goodbye.

00:48.300 --> 00:50.190
That's pretty much what we did.

00:50.190 --> 00:53.250
Okay, so now I'm gonna make a new branch from here.

00:53.250 --> 00:55.654
So git switch dash c,

00:55.654 --> 00:57.480
and I'm gonna just call this branch rainbow.

00:57.480 --> 01:00.420
It's where I'm gonna demo, demo some things.

01:00.420 --> 01:03.630
And then on this branch, I'm gonna start

01:03.630 --> 01:07.230
by getting rid of the background color in the body.

01:07.230 --> 01:09.240
Just have no background color.

01:09.240 --> 01:12.660
And again, if you don't know CSS, it's totally okay,

01:12.660 --> 01:14.520
but hopefully you can see when I wrote magenta,

01:14.520 --> 01:16.440
we had a magenta background.

01:16.440 --> 01:19.440
And I'm just going to leave it at that for now,

01:19.440 --> 01:20.940
and I'm gonna commit that.

01:20.940 --> 01:24.630
So git add app dot CSS git commit, you know,

01:24.630 --> 01:26.643
remove background color.

01:27.570 --> 01:30.180
Okay, so nothing in the stash right now,

01:30.180 --> 01:32.550
and we don't have any changes that we could put in there.

01:32.550 --> 01:34.440
But now I'm gonna make a single change.

01:34.440 --> 01:39.440
I'm going to give the body a background color of red,

01:39.780 --> 01:41.700
and I'm going to go in the order of a rainbow,

01:41.700 --> 01:44.040
or at least like the standard, you know

01:44.040 --> 01:47.163
roygbv, red, orange, yellow, green, blue, so on.

01:48.330 --> 01:50.283
So, we've got red.

01:51.720 --> 01:52.860
Just refresh the page.

01:52.860 --> 01:55.590
There it is, red background, but I'm not gonna commit this.

01:55.590 --> 01:57.540
I'm gonna add it to the stash.

01:57.540 --> 02:00.780
So git stash, okay.

02:00.780 --> 02:04.800
And now we're back to just an empty app dot CSS.

02:04.800 --> 02:07.710
And if I refresh my page, we have a white background.

02:07.710 --> 02:09.930
Now I'm gonna stash again, but this time,

02:09.930 --> 02:14.610
I'm gonna set the body to have a background color of orange.

02:14.610 --> 02:15.930
So that's what it looks like.

02:15.930 --> 02:18.240
I'm not gonna add and commit.

02:18.240 --> 02:21.030
And Git tells me, hey, you modified that file.

02:21.030 --> 02:23.763
I'm just gonna stash it right here, get stash.

02:24.750 --> 02:25.800
And there we are.

02:25.800 --> 02:29.130
We have another thing on the stash, the change is reverted

02:29.130 --> 02:31.740
in my working directory, we go back to white here.

02:31.740 --> 02:34.110
So I'll do it one more time, body.

02:34.110 --> 02:36.510
Okay, so now background color yellow on the body.

02:36.510 --> 02:37.890
That's what it looks like.

02:37.890 --> 02:41.940
And once again, we have some unstaged changes.

02:41.940 --> 02:43.623
I'm going to stash them.

02:44.550 --> 02:47.670
Okay, so now we have three things in the stash.

02:47.670 --> 02:49.260
They're very simple, right?

02:49.260 --> 02:50.580
Three sets of changes.

02:50.580 --> 02:53.490
And the first thing was just giving the background color

02:53.490 --> 02:55.110
of the body or making it red.

02:55.110 --> 02:57.060
Then the second thing I stashed was orange

02:57.060 --> 02:59.160
and the third was yellow.

02:59.160 --> 03:02.970
So they're stored in order and we can view what we have

03:02.970 --> 03:06.843
in the stash if needed using git stash list.

03:07.740 --> 03:12.740
So if I head back over here, git stash list, there they are.

03:13.290 --> 03:15.780
We have, well actually, we have four things

03:15.780 --> 03:18.650
in the stash because when I used apply earlier,

03:18.650 --> 03:21.660
in the previous video when I demonstrated how apply works,

03:21.660 --> 03:24.900
I never actually popped that set of changes off the stash.

03:24.900 --> 03:26.280
So we still have that here,

03:26.280 --> 03:29.460
but we have three that we just added.

03:29.460 --> 03:31.830
Now notice, it gives us, it says work

03:31.830 --> 03:34.440
in progress on branch rainbow in our case.

03:34.440 --> 03:37.200
And then it gives us the most recent commit,

03:37.200 --> 03:40.200
where we were working when we made that stash.

03:40.200 --> 03:41.640
Remove background color.

03:41.640 --> 03:44.640
So this doesn't really help us in any way, but to be honest,

03:44.640 --> 03:47.100
it would be really weird to do what I just did,

03:47.100 --> 03:49.800
to make three, or to stash, three sets

03:49.800 --> 03:52.980
of changes on the same branch, one after another.

03:52.980 --> 03:54.930
You would probably just make those changes

03:54.930 --> 03:58.080
and stash them, or work on a different branch, right?

03:58.080 --> 03:59.370
You, you wouldn't do what I just did,

03:59.370 --> 04:01.140
