04:01.140 --> 04:05.400
So, if I do git stash pop, for example,

04:05.400 --> 04:09.240
we will be popping this off and applying those changes.

04:09.240 --> 04:11.010
So I, maybe I don't want that.

04:11.010 --> 04:13.740
If I want red, which is this one here,

04:13.740 --> 04:15.720
this was the first one that we added

04:15.720 --> 04:17.610
from this branch, rainbow.

04:17.610 --> 04:20.400
I actually can reference particular stashes

04:20.400 --> 04:23.550
by using the little stash id.

04:23.550 --> 04:25.560
So it looks like this, git stash,

04:25.560 --> 04:27.630
and then I can do apply

04:27.630 --> 04:29.970
and then reference the particular stash.

04:29.970 --> 04:33.540
Stash at two inside of those curly braces.

04:33.540 --> 04:36.300
So I'll do stash at two right here.

04:36.300 --> 04:40.290
That should be our red background color.

04:40.290 --> 04:41.970
And if you're confused by this, honestly,

04:41.970 --> 04:43.560
I just say let it go.

04:43.560 --> 04:45.120
It's okay.

04:45.120 --> 04:47.490
Just focus on git stash and git stash pop.

04:47.490 --> 04:50.220
But, here we are, type git status.

04:50.220 --> 04:52.530
We don't have any background color here,

04:52.530 --> 04:54.810
but, if I do git stash apply,

04:54.810 --> 04:59.810
and then that stash at two in curly braces, okay,

05:00.210 --> 05:04.230
we now have modified app CSS, and there it is, it's red.

05:04.230 --> 05:06.150
Refresh the page, we see red.

05:06.150 --> 05:08.250
Now if instead I applied a different stash,

05:08.250 --> 05:10.770
can go back, git stash list.

05:10.770 --> 05:14.100
If we look at this one here, stash one,

05:14.100 --> 05:17.760
that's going to be the orange background color.

05:17.760 --> 05:21.900
And if I try to apply that one right now, git stash one,

05:21.900 --> 05:24.300
we run into a conflict, right?

05:24.300 --> 05:27.300
There's a problem because it's set to red right now

05:27.300 --> 05:29.160
and that is unstaged.

05:29.160 --> 05:31.350
So I either need to get rid of that change,

05:31.350 --> 05:34.500
which I could do, I could just delete the whole thing,

05:34.500 --> 05:37.590
type git status and we're back to where we were before

05:37.590 --> 05:40.650
and now I can apply this other stash, right.

05:40.650 --> 05:42.900
And it changes to orange, okay.

05:42.900 --> 05:46.230
And really, that's enough of, of showing you this.

05:46.230 --> 05:49.170
The point is that we can have multiple things in the stash

05:49.170 --> 05:50.130
at once.

05:50.130 --> 05:53.700
In my experience, I pretty much rarely, I won't say never,

05:53.700 --> 05:55.410
